{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-9644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/assets/c06da8f06e8d640c23dbd81885fdd1bd5e5d89b15b1729cacd82ac52f301e44d.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r={e}^{3\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-9644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )={e}^{3\\theta }$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=2\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{({e}^{3\\theta })}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{e}^{6\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{e}^{6\\theta }{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}({e}^{12\\pi }-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}({e}^{12\\pi }-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-9644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0320bd4e27f24258a630079054486a91d58178ac20655961be15ce6c83ba7e6"} {"question" "q-9644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-9644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{12}({e}^{12\\pi }-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}({e}^{3\\pi }-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}({e}^{6\\pi }-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{6\\pi }-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}({e}^{12\\pi }-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-9644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}({e}^{12\\pi }-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-124201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/assets/34f6562d5a661d3a58755622571f50752aefa11c8e58b85dad5c70b13c179746.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r={e}^{\\theta +1}$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-124201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )={e}^{\\theta +1}$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{({e}^{\\theta +1})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\theta +2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\theta +2}{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2\\pi +2}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{2}({e}^{2\\pi }-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-124201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0320bd4e27f24258a630079054486a91d58178ac20655961be15ce6c83ba7e6"} {"question" "q-124201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-124201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}({e}^{2\\pi }-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}({e}^{\\pi +2}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2\\pi }-2)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}e({e}^{2\\pi }-2)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{2}({e}^{2\\pi }-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-124201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{2}({e}^{2\\pi }-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/assets/09b9f122e75f9d04d4bade197e57a319bc058b0ec22bcf3e35a9feab080c9f1c.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=4-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=4-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(4-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(16-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(16-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(18\\theta +16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(18\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}+16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}) \\\\  & =9\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =9(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})+8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}+8(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0320bd4e27f24258a630079054486a91d58178ac20655961be15ce6c83ba7e6"} {"question" "q-352316" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352316" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9\\pi}{2}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta -\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}){|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi +2}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0320bd4e27f24258a630079054486a91d58178ac20655961be15ce6c83ba7e6"} {"question" "q-352332" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352332" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{8}+\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{3}{2}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{3}{2}\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{4}){|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{3}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{4}\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\,) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{8}\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))-\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-(0-0)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0320bd4e27f24258a630079054486a91d58178ac20655961be15ce6c83ba7e6"} {"question" "q-352344" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066449/state.json" "file_sha256" "c501f239386aa33a7ec6f65837c4fb11dfb2f509d06d5247bef0c20601635c8b"} {"question" "q-352344" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-